Well, you could rationalise the death drop a bit by arguing that they
were always carrying the stuff, just not using it. However, a wand of
probing would prove you wrong.

If you think the death drop is irrational, consider that there's another
just as irrational thing: the random creation of monsters. They just
appear out of nowhere (though out of sight). If you're blindfolded, they
might be created out of the blue, next to you.

Even if the death drop were abolished, it would still in a way be there
if monsters were still "dropped". You'd have to have monsters created
only when a level was newly created, and no more monsters being randomly
created anymore. Of course, monster creation by kicking sinks, create
monster, etc. would still be valid.

